1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:01,807
A week ago my friend,

2
00:00:01,807 --> 00:00:03,154
an underwriter, cancelled our

3
00:00:03,154 --> 00:00:03,607
road trip.

4
00:00:03,607 --> 00:00:06,007
He was buried in bank statements.

5
00:00:06,007 --> 00:00:08,944
His fear about AI wasn't speed.

6
00:00:08,944 --> 00:00:09,769
It was this:

7
00:00:09,769 --> 00:00:11,464
"If it makes up a number,

8
00:00:11,464 --> 00:00:14,150
it's my name on the file."

9
00:00:14,150 --> 00:00:16,008
So I started building a tool

10
00:00:16,008 --> 00:00:17,424
for him with Bridgie,

11
00:00:17,424 --> 00:00:19,986
my AI agent team.

12
00:00:19,986 --> 00:00:21,251
First, Bridgie interviewed

13
00:00:21,251 --> 00:00:21,681
me.

14
00:00:21,681 --> 00:00:23,295
Seventy-six questions.

15
00:00:23,295 --> 00:00:24,607
Then it wrote a spec:

16
00:00:24,607 --> 00:00:26,580
fifty-five requirements, twenty

17
00:00:26,580 --> 00:00:28,264
rules that must always hold,

18
00:00:28,264 --> 00:00:30,691
and forty-one tasks.

19
00:00:30,691 --> 00:00:32,061
You could prompt an AI into

20
00:00:32,061 --> 00:00:33,489
a demo in an afternoon.

21
00:00:33,489 --> 00:00:34,766
But you couldn't prove a single

22
00:00:34,766 --> 00:00:36,294
number in it.

23
00:00:36,294 --> 00:00:38,570
In Bridgie, a task isn't done

24
00:00:38,570 --> 00:00:40,160
when the AI says so.

25
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:41,704
It passes the tests,

26
00:00:41,704 --> 00:00:43,423
then a reviewer from a different

27
00:00:43,423 --> 00:00:45,466
AI company tries to break it,

28
00:00:45,466 --> 00:00:47,695
then a human signs.

29
00:00:47,695 --> 00:00:49,204
The statement reader alone

30
00:00:49,204 --> 00:00:50,981
took sixty-five rounds.

31
00:00:50,981 --> 00:00:52,397
It caught a fraction of a

32
00:00:52,397 --> 00:00:53,988
penny lost to rounding,

33
00:00:53,988 --> 00:00:56,159
a refund counted as income,

34
00:00:56,159 --> 00:00:57,772
a file that crashed instead

35
00:00:57,772 --> 00:01:00,311
of naming the bad line.

36
00:01:00,311 --> 00:01:01,507
A week in,

37
00:01:01,507 --> 00:01:03,968
nineteen of forty-one are done.

38
00:01:03,968 --> 00:01:05,710
Statements read to the penny,

39
00:01:05,710 --> 00:01:07,416
every figure traceable to its

40
00:01:07,416 --> 00:01:09,216
transactions, nothing leaving

41
00:01:09,216 --> 00:01:11,158
the laptop.

42
00:01:11,158 --> 00:01:12,586
Not released yet,

43
00:01:12,586 --> 00:01:14,629
and no underwriter has used

44
00:01:14,629 --> 00:01:17,279
it on real work yet.

45
00:01:17,279 --> 00:01:18,951
Nineteen of forty-one isn't

46
00:01:18,951 --> 00:01:19,346
slow.

47
00:01:19,346 --> 00:01:22,505
It's what "I'd sign this" costs.
